to build this ohmmeter youll need materials and specifically the 4 resistors mentioned in the 
code. a 1000ohm, 10000ohm, 100000ohm, and 1000000ohm resistors

Reference resistors:

- connect these resistors from the digital pins in the order that they are in the code to a breadboard
- connect the other end of the resistors to a line on a breadboard
- connect this line to the A0 analog pin so they are all able to be used as reference resistors
- this connects the group of resistors together at the end so that the connection point between them 
and the test resisotr can be measured to find Vout

Test resistor:

- connect one end of the test resistor to the ground pin
- connect the other end of the test resistor to the same A0 analog pin line on the bread board
- this completes the voltage divider circuit that is used in the code
- the known input voltage, output voltage, and resistor values complets the equation to solve for the test resistor
- the code then uses each of the resitors in order then cuts out the test resistor values that are 
the least accurate based on voltage output

you can then attach the ends of any resistor between 200 and 4.5 million ohms for most accurate readings 
as the lower and upper ends are inaccurate

Design in TinkerCad:
https://www.tinkercad.com/things/absR6OP9mc8-ohmmeter-better/editel?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tinkercad.com%2Fdashboard%2Fdesigns%2Fall
